The following errata report has been rejected for RFC8446,
"The Transport Layer Security (TLS) Protocol Version 1.3".

--------------------------------------
You may review the report below and at:
https://www.rfc-editor.org/errata/eid6143

--------------------------------------
Status: Rejected
Type: Technical

Reported by: Ben Smyth <research@bensmyth.com>
Date Reported: 2020-04-29
Rejected by: Paul Wouters (IESG)

Section: 4.2.7

Original Text
-------------
As of TLS 1.3, servers are permitted to send the "supported_groups"
extension to the client.

Corrected Text
--------------


Notes
-----
It is unclear whether servers are permitted to send the "supported_groups" extension to 
the client without solicitation, i.e., when the client does not first send the extension to the 
server. Clarification would be useful.
 --VERIFIER NOTES-- 
   rejected by WG

